{
  "response": "# Verdict: REJECT\n\n**Overall Assessment**:  \nThe `BuggyMegaMenu` component represents a complete accessibility failure. Built entirely out of unstyled, non-semantic `<div>` elements with bare `onClick` listeners, it contains zero keyboard focusability, no landmark or list semantics, no ARIA disclosure/menu pattern support, and zero programmatic state communication. For any keyboard-only or screen reader user, this component is entirely invisible and inoperable.\n\n---\n\n### Pre-commitment Predictions\nBefore reviewing the code, typical issues predicted for custom mega menus / dropdown navigations were:\n1. Missing `<nav>` landmark and `<ul>`/`<li>` list semantics.\n2. Trigger elements rendered as `<div>` or `<span>` instead of native `<button>`.\n3. Missing `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls` on the menu triggers.\n4. Absence of keyboard event handlers (Enter, Space, Escape, Arrow keys).\n5. No focus restoration to the trigger when closing submenus.\n\n*Outcome:* All predictions were confirmed; the component lacks even the most fundamental baseline HTML semantics and keyboard hooks.\n\n---\n\n## Findings\n\n### Critical Findings (Blocks Access)\n\n1. **Non-interactive `<div>` with `onClick` completely excludes keyboard-only and switch-control users**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyMegaMenu.jsx:10-14`\n   - **Element**: `<div className=\"menu-item\" onClick={...}>`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Keyboard-only, switch device, screen reader users\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard (Level A), WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (Level A)\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: A `<div>` is neither focusable nor keyboard-activatable by default. A keyboard user pressing `Tab` will skip right over every top-level menu item. Pressing `Enter` or `Space` produces no action. This completely blocks keyboard users from navigating beyond the first page.\n   - **Fix**: Replace `<div className=\"menu-item\">` with a semantic `<button type=\"button\">` or contain an explicit `<button>` trigger within an `<li>` item.\n\n2. **Zero state communication for submenu expansion to assistive technology**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyMegaMenu.jsx:14-25`\n   - **Element**: Trigger `<div className=\"menu-item\">` and dropdown container `<div className=\"submenu\">`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users (VoiceOver, NVDA, JAWS)\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (Level A), WAI-ARIA APG Disclosure (Show/Hide) or Menu Button Pattern\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: When a menu expands, nothing informs assistive technology that an expandable region exists, nor whether it is collapsed or open. Screen readers announce only raw text with no clue that children exist or that clicking will reveal additional links.\n   - **Fix**: Add `aria-expanded={openMenu === idx}` and `aria-controls={`submenu-${idx}`}` to the trigger button, and provide `id={`submenu-${idx}`}` on the submenu container.\n\n3. **Submenu items lack interactive semantics and focusability**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyMegaMenu.jsx:18-22`\n   - **Element**: `<div key={cidx} className=\"submenu-item\">{child}</div>`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Keyboard-only, screen reader, cognitive users\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard (Level A), WCAG 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (Level A)\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: Even if a user clicks with a mouse to open the submenu, the children are rendered inside generic `<div>` tags. Unless `{child}` itself happens to be an anchor or button (which is unmanaged and unenforced), these submenu items cannot be focused, tabbed through, or operated.\n   - **Fix**: Render child items inside list items (`<li>`) containing native focusable links (`<a>`) or buttons (`<button>`).\n\n---\n\n### Major Findings (Significantly Degrades Experience)\n\n1. **Complete absence of landmark and list navigation structure (\"Div Soup\")**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyMegaMenu.jsx:7-9`\n   - **Element**: `<div className=\"megamenu-container\">` and `<div className=\"megamenu-items\">`\n   - **Impacted Group**: Screen reader users\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 1.3.1 Info and Relationships (Level A), WCAG 2.4.1 Bypass Blocks (Level A)\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: Without `<nav aria-label=\"...\">` and `<ul>`/`<li>` hierarchy, screen reader users cannot discover the navigation via landmark jump shortcuts (e.g., `D` in JAWS/NVDA) and lose hierarchical context (e.g., \"Menu, 5 items\").\n   - **Fix**: Wrap the container in a `<nav aria-label=\"Main Navigation\">` and structure items as unordered lists (`<ul className=\"megamenu-items\">` with `<li className=\"menu-item\">`).\n\n2. **Missing keyboard dismissal (`Escape` key) and focus restoration**\n   - **Location**: `BuggyMegaMenu.jsx:11-13`\n   - **Element**: State handling (`setOpenMenu`)\n   - **Impacted Group**: Keyboard-only, low vision, cognitive users\n   - **WCAG / APG Citation**: WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard (Level A), WAI-ARIA APG Navigation Menubar / Disclosure\n   - **Confidence**: HIGH\n   - **Why this matters**: Once opened, there is no way for keyboard users to collapse the submenu without tabbing all the way out or clicking elsewhere. There is no `onKeyDown` handler listening for `Escape` to close the menu and return focus to the top-level trigger.\n   - **Fix**: Attach an `onKeyDown` listener to handle `Escape`. When pressed, call `setOpenMenu(null)` and return focus to the trigger element via a `ref`.\n\n---\n\n### Measured Evidence Finding\n\n```yaml\n### A11y Evidence Finding\nfinding_id: megamenu_div_click_operability\nfingerprint: 7f8a1c93b2e45d10\nsource: BuggyMegaMenu.jsx:10-14\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard (Level A), WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value\nsection_508_fpc_context: WCAG 2.0 A/AA \u00a71194.22(a)\nseverity: CRITICAL\nperspective_alarms: screen_reader=HIGH, keyboard_only=HIGH, low_vision=MEDIUM, cognitive=MEDIUM\nevidence: \"<div key={idx} className=\\\"menu-item\\\" onClick={() => setOpenMenu(openMenu === idx ? null : idx)}>\"\nreproduction_steps: \n  - Mount BuggyMegaMenu in browser or DOM test harness.\n  - Attempt to reach menu items using the Tab key.\n  - Observe that focus bypasses the component completely.\nexpected_behavior: \"All top-level menu triggers must be focusable via Tab and activatable with Enter and Space.\"\nactual_behavior: \"Elements are skipped during keyboard navigation; elements lack role='button' and tabindex.\"\ntrend: new\n```\n\n---\n\n### Minor Findings & Enhancements\n\n- **Minor**: Click outside to dismiss is not handled. Mouse and screen magnifier users who open a large mega-menu cannot easily close it without clicking the exact same trigger element again.\n- **Enhancement**: Add `aria-current=\"page\"` support if items link to routes, allowing users to know which section they are currently viewing.\n\n---\n\n### What's Missing\n\n- **Native interactive triggers**: Requisite `<button>` or `<a>` elements.\n- **Semantic structure**: `<nav>`, `<ul>`, `<li>`.\n- **WAI-ARIA disclosure attributes**: `aria-expanded=\"true|false\"`, `aria-controls=\"[id]\"`, `aria-haspopup=\"true\"`.\n- **Keyboard interaction model**:\n  - `Enter` / `Space` to toggle dropdowns.\n  - `Escape` to close the currently open dropdown and refocus trigger.\n  - `ArrowDown` / `ArrowUp` or standard sequential `Tab` order through open child items.\n- **Outside click / blur listener**: Submenus remain open indefinitely until another trigger is activated.\n\n---\n\n### Perspective Alarm Levels\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|:---|:---:|:---|\n| Screen reader | **HIGH** | Complete absence of roles, landmarks, list structure, and dynamic states |\n| Keyboard-only | **HIGH** | Component is 100% unnavigable with Tab or standard activation keys |\n| Low vision | **MEDIUM** | Inability to dismiss overlay, missing focus indicators on custom elements |\n| Cognitive | **MEDIUM** | Inconsistent behavior, lack of predictable keyboard shortcuts |\n| Vestibular & motion | **LOW** | No animation or motion currently implemented |\n| Auditory access | **LOW** | No audio or video content present |\n| Environmental contrast | **MEDIUM** | Custom CSS class dependencies; contrast cannot be evaluated without styles |\n\n---\n\n### Multi-Perspective Notes\n\n- **Screen Reader User**: A screen reader will announce only raw text strings without identifying that this is navigation or a menu. There is no feedback indicating that an item is expandable, whether it is open or closed, or how many sub-items exist.\n- **Keyboard-Only User**: Completely blocked. The browser\u2019s focus mechanism skips every item. Keyboard users cannot access any link or content inside the submenu.\n- **Low Vision User**: Users who navigate magnified at 200\u2013400% zoom rely heavily on predictable focus indicators and the ability to dismiss large popover menus using `Escape`. Without focus cues, they get lost.\n- **Cognitive Accessibility**: Unpredictable and fragile click targets without clear affordances or keyboard alternatives cause disorientation.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Remediation\n\nRefactor the component to use semantic HTML and the **WAI-ARIA APG Disclosure Navigation Menu** pattern:\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useRef } from 'react';\n\nconst AccessibleMegaMenu = ({ items = [] }) => {\n  const [openMenu, setOpenMenu] = useState(null);\n  const triggerRefs = useRef([]);\n\n  const handleKeyDown = (e, idx) => {\n    if (e.key === 'Escape' && openMenu === idx) {\n      setOpenMenu(null);\n      triggerRefs.current[idx]?.focus();\n    }\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <nav aria-label=\"Main Navigation\" className=\"megamenu-container\">\n      <ul className=\"megamenu-items\">\n        {items.map((item, idx) => {\n          const isOpen = openMenu === idx;\n          const submenuId = `submenu-${idx}`;\n\n          return (\n            <li key={idx} className=\"menu-item\" onKeyDown={(e) => handleKeyDown(e, idx)}>\n              <button\n                type=\"button\"\n                ref={(el) => (triggerRefs.current[idx] = el)}\n                aria-expanded={isOpen}\n                aria-controls={submenuId}\n                aria-haspopup=\"true\"\n                onClick={() => setOpenMenu(isOpen ? null : idx)}\n              >\n                {item.label}\n              </button>\n\n              {isOpen && (\n                <ul id={submenuId} className=\"submenu\">\n                  {item.children &&\n                    item.children.map((child, cidx) => (\n                      <li key={cidx} className=\"submenu-item\">\n                        {child}\n                      </li>\n                    ))}\n                </ul>\n              )}\n            </li>\n          );\n        })}\n      </ul>\n    </nav>\n  );\n};\n\nexport default AccessibleMegaMenu;\n```\n\n---\n\n### Verdict Justification\n**REJECT**: This code cannot be shipped. It violates WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard), WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value), and WCAG 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships) at Level A. To reach `ACCEPT`, the component must replace non-semantic `<div>` elements with `<nav>`, `<ul>`, `<li>`, and `<button>`, implement `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`, and introduce basic keyboard controls (`Escape`, `Enter`, `Space`).\n",
